```
def bubbleSort(arr):
    n = len(arr)

    for i in range(n-1):
        for j in range(0, n-i-1):
            if arr[j] > arr[j+1]:
                arr[j], arr[j+1] = arr[j+1], arr[j]

arr = [56, 45, 23, 17, 87, 32, 12]
bubbleSort(arr)

print("Sorted array is:")
for i in range(len(arr)):
    print("%d" % arr[i], end=" ")
```

This implementation of the bubble sort algorithm compares adjacent elements of the input array and swaps them until no more swaps are required. The resulting sorted array is [12 17 23 32 45 56 87].

